for america's fossil fuel lobby this is  a major prize they've robbed president  biden of his main tool for cutting  carbon emissions from u.s power plants  the supreme court ruled 6-3 against the  u.s environmental protection agency not  stripping it of pollution controlling  powers but preventing them being used  against an entire fuel type  conservative lobbyists are delighted  what it did say was that the the epa did  not have the power to destroy the coal  industry for something as politically  and economically significant as that it  needs clear direction from congress and  certainly that direction has not been  given  a total of 18 states and two coal mining  companies joined west virginia in  bringing this action many are top coal  producing states and no surprise nearly  all of them are republican-led and it  matters because over half of u.s  electricity is generated by fossil fuels  mainly coal and gas so it's a major  setback for joe biden's 2050 net zero  target but not a complete loss firstly  look here at coal even through the trump  era coal use was coming steadily down  through the early since the early 2000s  and today's ruling doesn't diminish  individual states authority to regulate  emissions there are 21 states with net  zero targets of their own and their own  rules to close coal and gas power plants  based on sure economics we're seeing  coal becoming increasingly uneconomic  and renewable energy battery storage are  becoming cheaper by the day and there's  a big uptake but it's not happening fast  enough not on the scale necessary and  federal action is critical to securing  the scale of that progress as quickly as  we need it  today's victory was secured in part by  donald trump who as well as digging coal  loaded the supreme court with  conservative judges  despite their best efforts fossil fuels  are on the way out question is will  today's ruling prevent them from going  fast enough to prevent dangerous climate  change  tom clark sky news
 

